### Slide 21 — Detached HEAD in Worktrees ⭐

```bash
# Specific commit SHA
git worktree add --detach ./review-v1 a1b2c3d4
git worktree add -d ./review-v1 a1b2c3d4

# Version tag
git worktree add -d ./review-v2.0 v2.0.0

# 3 commits before HEAD
git worktree add -d ./review-previous HEAD~3
```

```
/path/portfolio/main           abc1234  [main]
/path/portfolio/review-v2.0    def5678  (detached HEAD)
```

**Use cases:**
- Review old code without affecting any branch
- Run tests against a specific released version
- Debug regressions side-by-side

> ⚠️ Avoid committing from detached HEAD — commits not on any branch
> can be lost during garbage collection.
> If needed: `git switch -c my-branch`

